  "step_3": "First, the information relevant to the decision reason includes: (1) identifying probable outcomes based on the 1/n threshold (n = number of outcomes), and (2) computing the average of those probable outcomes. In this case, both lotteries have only 0 Euros as a probable outcome, so their average is 0, leading to indifference. The individual did not consider this categorization or calculation. Second, the individual’s justification is based on comparing the worst-case loss (-4000 vs. -6000) and acknowledging a higher chance of loss in B, but they do not refer to any probabilistic categorization of outcomes or averaging. Their reasoning is based on the magnitude of losses and subjective feelings of randomness, not on the rule of averaging probable outcomes. Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual applied the decision reason. The reasoning process described is fundamentally different from the decision reason’s rule. The individual did not use the reason to make the decision.",
